\label{lemma-flat-base-change-lci}
A flat base change of a local complete intersection morphism is a
local complete intersection morphism.

\label{lemma-regular-at-x}
Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$.
Let $x \in |X|$ be a point. The following are equivalent
\begin{enumerate}
\item $X$ is regular at $x$, and
\item the \'etale local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ is
regular for any (equivalently some) geometric point $\overline{x}$
lying over $x$.
\end{enumerate}

\label{lemma-smooth-quotient-morphism}
Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid in functors on $\mathcal{C}_\Lambda$.
The following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item The groupoid in functors $(U, R, s, t, c)$ is smooth.
\item The morphism $s : R \to U$ is smooth.
\item The morphism $t : R \to U$ is smooth.
\item The quotient morphism $U \to [U/R]$ is smooth.
\end{enumerate}

